{"id":"windows/settings/folder-home-pages-for-outlook-special-folders","platform":"windows","kind":"csp","surface":"settings","identifier":"folder-home-pages-for-outlook-special-folders","name":"Folder Home Pages for Outlook Special Folders","description":"Windows MDM settings in the Folder Home Pages for Outlook Special Folders category, applied as OMA-URI (SyncML) values.","group":"Microsoft Outlook 2016","properties":[{"key":"L_CalendarFolderHomePage","name":"Calendar Folder Home Page (User)","type":"enum","description":"This policy setting allows you to modify the \"Show home page by default for this folder\" in the Home Page tab of the Calendar Properties dialog box.\n\nIf you enable this policy setting, you will set the \"Show home page by default for this folder\" check box. You will also be able to enter a URL, which has a maximum limit of 129 characters.\n\nIf you disable or do not configure this policy setting, the \"Show home page by default for this folder\" check box will not be checked.","defaultValue":0,"enum":[{"value":"0","description":"Disabled"},{"value":"1","description":"Enabled"}],"address":"./User/Vendor/MSFT/Policy/Config/outlk16v2~Policy~L_MicrosoftOfficeOutlook~L_FolderHomePagesforOutlookspecialfolders/L_CalendarFolderHomePage","scope":"user","introducedIn":"CSP 5.0","source":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/client-management/mdm/policy-csp-outlk16v2"},{"key":"L_ContactsFolderHomePage","name":"Contacts Folder Home Page (User)","type":"enum","description":"This policy setting allows you to modify the \"Show home page by default for this folder\" in the Home Page tab of the Contacts Properties dialog box.\n\nIf you enable this policy setting, you will set the \"Show home page by default for this folder\" check box. You will also be able to enter a URL, which has a maximum limit of 129 characters.\n\nIf you disable or do not configure this policy setting, the \"Show home page by default for this folder\" check box will not be checked.","defaultValue":0,"enum":[{"value":"0","description":"Disabled"},{"value":"1","description":"Enabled"}],"address":"./User/Vendor/MSFT/Policy/Config/outlk16v2~Policy~L_MicrosoftOfficeOutlook~L_FolderHomePagesforOutlookspecialfolders/L_ContactsFolderHomePage","scope":"user","introducedIn":"CSP 5.0","source":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/client-management/mdm/policy-csp-outlk16v2"},{"key":"L_DeletedItemsFolderHomePage","name":"Deleted Items Folder Home Page (User)","type":"enum","description":"This policy setting allows you to modify the \"Show home page by default for this folder\" in the Home Page tab of the Deleted Items Properties dialog box.\n\nIf you enable this policy setting, you will set the \"Show home page by default for this folder\" check box. You will also be able to enter a URL, which has a maximum limit of 129 characters.\n\nIf you disable or do not configure this policy setting, the \"Show home page by default for this folder\" check box will not be checked.","defaultValue":0,"enum":[{"value":"0","description":"Disabled"},{"value":"1","description":"Enabled"}],"address":"./User/Vendor/MSFT/Policy/Config/outlk16v2~Policy~L_MicrosoftOfficeOutlook~L_FolderHomePagesforOutlookspecialfolders/L_DeletedItemsFolderHomePage","scope":"user","introducedIn":"CSP 5.0","source":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/client-management/mdm/policy-csp-outlk16v2"},{"key":"L_DisableFolderHomePages","name":"Do not allow Home Page URL to be set in folder Properties (User)","type":"enum","description":"By default, users can set a URL to be used as the Home Page for a folder by entering the URL on the Home Page tab on the folder's Properties dialog box. By enabling this setting, you can disallow setting Folder Home Pages for all folders.","defaultValue":0,"enum":[{"value":"0","description":"Disabled"},{"value":"1","description":"Enabled"}],"address":"./User/Vendor/MSFT/Policy/Config/outlk16v2~Policy~L_MicrosoftOfficeOutlook~L_FolderHomePagesforOutlookspecia